      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Storing high volumes of flammable industrial solvents in high-density racking systems poses significant risks related to thermal runaway, vapor accumulation, and structural integrity during a thermal event. In a high-density setup, poor air circulation can lead to dangerous vapor accumulation, making the environment highly flammable. Additionally, if a fire occurs, inhomogeneous heating may result in thermal runaway, where insulation regimes fail and heat is transferred more rapidly, potentially leading to violent and uncontrollable fires. The dense materials used for racking may also suffer reduced integrity under high temperatures, especially when solvents are present because their presence can subdue material strength, thus compromising the rack structure and increasing the risk of collapse. Firefighting efforts could be further complicated due to the volatile and explosive nature of the concentrated vapors.",
